Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.75,0:00:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.55,0:00:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Darts!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.87,0:00:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You were expecting someone else?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.33,0:00:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I want my company\Nback, so can the small talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.57,0:00:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,As for me, I want your souls for my wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.07,0:00:18.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Then let's stop talking and\Nstart dueling! Not alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.43,0:00:20.75,Default,,0,0,0,,This lunatic is far too dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.11,0:00:22.64,Default,,0,0,0,,So why don't you join him?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.79,0:00:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,And when I defeat you, I'll get\Ntwo souls for the price of one!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.35,0:00:30.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold, a power that has\Nexisted since the dawn of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.89,0:00:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Arise, Orychalcos Gaius!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.37,0:00:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Master of Dragon Soldier!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.87,0:00:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.65,0:00:43.65,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.89,0:00:49.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You're getting a glimpse of the legendary\Ncity of Atlantis when I ruled as king!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.29,0:00:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You were king?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.69,0:00:52.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed, I was.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.37,0:00:54.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And I shall be once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.09,0:00:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,For when I defeat you,\Nparadise shall return!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.77,0:01:37.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.31,0:02:09.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold, the lost city of Atlantis in all\Nits glory, just as it was 10,000 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.53,0:02:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,A perfect civilization, or so I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.47,0:02:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Surrounded by ocean, as\Nfar as the eye could see,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.53,0:02:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,we were isolated from\Nthe rest of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.41,0:02:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Our lives were simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.65,0:02:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We existed side by side with\Nall of Earth's creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.67,0:02:34.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And we knew nothing of violence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.15,0:02:36.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But then, that changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.39,0:02:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Darkness descended upon us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.01,0:02:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And a strange substance\Nrained down from the heavens.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.03,0:02:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,A substance that would change our lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.23,0:02:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The Orycalcus.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.61,0:02:58.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Please tell me that story time is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.99,0:03:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.61,0:03:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,The tale of my past directly\Naffects the fate of your future.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.05,0:03:08.83,Default,,0,0,0,,So if I were you, I'd pay close attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.95,0:03:10.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.91,0:03:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,thanks to the stones of the Orycalcus,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.29,0:03:15.45,Default,,0,0,0,,the people of Atlantis\Nmade advancements in
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.53,0:03:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,technology that were\Nnever before imagined.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.83,0:03:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And soon,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.55,0:03:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I ruled over the most highly developed\Ncivilization the world had ever known.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.33,0:03:29.97,Default,,0,0,0,,However, with progress comes\Ngreed and eventually violence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.47,0:03:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew what had to be done, but my father,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.65,0:03:36.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Former King Ironheart had different ideas.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.13,0:03:39.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Ironheart was your father? But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.87,0:03:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,If you ask questions, this\Nridiculous story's never gonna end.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.85,0:03:47.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That old fool never had\Nwhat it took to be king.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.83,0:03:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And on my 21st birthday, he allowed me to\Ntake over and fill his unimpressive shoes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.55,0:03:57.15,Default,,0,0,0,,So as technology continued to advance,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.47,0:04:01.61,Default,,0,0,0,,and the hearts of my people continued\Nto sink deeper into the darkness,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.69,0:04:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,it was up to me to remedy the situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.71,0:04:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The citizens of Atlantis were\Ngrowing more and more selfish,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.97,0:04:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and if I didn't act soon, I\Nwould lose complete control.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.83,0:04:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,But even I couldn't have\Nimagined what would happen next.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.83,0:04:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The Aurichalcos began to test us.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.21,0:04:22.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It revealed the truth about who we were.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.47,0:04:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Those who were wicked on the inside\Nbecame wicked on the outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.13,0:04:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Iona, are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.27,0:04:43.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait! Come back!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.07,0:04:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.57,0:04:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Iona!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.45,0:04:58.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't realize it at first,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.91,0:05:02.56,Default,,0,0,0,,but the true colors of my people\Nwere revealed to me that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.17,0:05:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.61,0:05:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is this happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.25,0:05:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn't understand how a society as\Nperfect as ours could crumble like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.09,0:05:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But soon the Orichalcos would\Nanswer all my questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.79,0:05:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The people of Atlantis were evil,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.31,0:05:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,and I had been chosen to wipe\Nthem out and start over again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.95,0:05:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,But I couldn't accomplish\Nsuch a task on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.47,0:05:52.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I was but one man, so the\NOrychalcos gave me a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.89,0:05:56.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Something powerful enough to\Nlead my fight against mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.89,0:05:59.01,Default,,0,0,0,,For deep below the Earth's surface lurked
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.09,0:06:01.74,Default,,0,0,0,,the most incredible\Ncreature that ever lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.87,0:06:03.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The Great Leviathan.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.09,0:06:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And it was mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.01,0:06:10.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And shortly this great beast will\Nreturn to finish what it began.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.83,0:06:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I was ready to begin my task of\Nrecreating civilization on Earth,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.07,0:06:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,but one person stood in my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.05,0:06:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,My son, you know what you have to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.03,0:06:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy those Orakalko stones so we\Ncan return to the life we once knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.67,0:06:37.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you honestly believe we can\Ngo back to the way things were?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.25,0:06:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It's too late for that, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.25,0:06:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,But darts...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.16,0:06:43.91,Default,,0,0,0,,The true nature of our\Npeople has been exposed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.03,0:06:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,We now know that the citizens of this\Nplanet are evil and must be destroyed. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.09,0:06:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You heard me, old man.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.63,0:06:54.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We should be thanking the\NOrychalcos for showing us the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.95,0:06:57.36,Default,,0,0,0,,not blaming it for the faults of mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.15,0:07:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, this mysterious substance that\Nrained down from above has opened up my eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.55,0:07:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only has it shown me\Nwhat's wrong with the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.01,0:07:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,it's given me the tools to fix it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.99,0:07:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,For I now have the power to awaken a mighty\Ncreature known as the Great Leviathan.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.79,0:07:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And by the power of the Orychalcos,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.35,0:07:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,this beast will rise up from the depths\Nof the earth and fight by my side.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.55,0:07:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And when I'm through, I\Nshall rebuild civilization.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.41,0:07:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Darts!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.32,0:07:37.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.97,0:07:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Meet my Orichalco soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.87,0:07:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, I'm scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.89,0:07:47.60,Default,,0,0,0,,If you join my side, you\Nhave nothing to fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.83,0:07:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,If not, then farewell.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.71,0:07:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll never join you. Never.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.31,0:07:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Chris.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.55,0:07:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Have it your way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.79,0:08:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,The time has come to cleanse\Nthe world of its impurities.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.67,0:08:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,So arise, my children, and\Nconquer the people of Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.25,0:08:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And this planet shall be yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.67,0:08:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What are we going to do, Grandpa?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.17,0:08:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Your father is under the control of\Nan evil force, and he must be stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.67,0:08:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The future of our planet depends on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.19,0:08:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Through there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.10,0:08:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.51,0:08:55.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.73,0:08:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are those monsters carved in stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.41,0:09:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,We've come here to ask for their help.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.39,0:09:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And so the Battle of Atlantis began. You\Nsee, my father had opened up a gateway to
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.55,0:09:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,the dominion of the beasts and he used the
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.11,0:09:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters within to form an army of his own
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.49,0:09:35.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me, what was the battle's outcome?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.33,0:09:40.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither side was victorious, and\NAtlantis sunk to the bottom of the sea.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.97,0:09:44.11,Default,,0,0,0,,My father's monster army\Nwas scattered around the
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.19,0:09:47.19,Default,,0,0,0,,world and sealed away until\Nthey'd be needed again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.11,0:09:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The Leviathan was drained of\Nhis power and also sealed away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.29,0:09:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It's taken me 10,000 years to gather\Nthe energy necessary to bring it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.63,0:10:01.21,Default,,0,0,0,,All that's left for me to do\Nis defeat you two in this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.71,0:10:03.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Then your souls will awaken the great
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.77,0:10:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Leviathan and my plan\Nwill finally come to pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.67,0:10:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.58,0:10:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,We already defeated you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.23,0:10:14.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Our Master of Dragon Soldier should have\Nwiped out the rest of your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.73,0:10:17.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps it should have,\Nbut I'm afraid it didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.79,0:10:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Your pathetic attack\Nfell short of its target.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.49,0:10:22.67,Default,,0,0,0,,So this duel's still on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.85,0:10:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, check it out! They're back! Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.51,0:10:35.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Seto!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.09,0:10:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.33,0:10:41.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You didn't lose one single life point!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.77,0:10:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Didn't I just tell you\Nyour attack didn't work?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.21,0:10:50.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to the special ability of my\NCutora, My damage was reduced to zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.77,0:10:52.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That's crazy!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.21,0:10:55.93,Default,,0,0,0,,He dodged an attack by\Ntheir strongest monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.01,0:10:58.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And what's worse, it's his turn now!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.39,0:11:01.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Orycalcos Gygas, return!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.59,0:11:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.31,0:11:07.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Each time his Pegasus is destroyed,\Nit comes back even stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.03,0:11:12.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Face it, you'll never defeat me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.01,0:11:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,The power of the Orycalcos\Nwill swallow you both.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.57,0:11:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Now back to the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.19,0:11:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Since my Giygas returned\Nto me, I can't draw a card.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.83,0:11:24.77,Default,,0,0,0,,But no matter, everything\NI need is in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.97,0:11:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,So I'll enhance the power\Nof the seal with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.55,0:11:31.19,Default,,0,0,0,,The magic of Orycalcos Deuteros!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.91,0:11:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.77,0:11:43.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Somehow he's made the seal\Nof Orycalcos stronger!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.25,0:12:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, welcome to the\Nsecond level of darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.21,0:12:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The what?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.63,0:12:19.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know how, but Dot just added\Nanother layer to the seal of Ory Kalkos.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.07,0:12:20.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.98,0:12:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,So what does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.27,0:12:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The first benefit of my Ory\NKalkos Duteros is the addition of
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.57,0:12:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,500 life points each turn for\Nevery monster I have on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.29,0:12:34.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Therefore, since I have two,\Nthat's 1,000 points. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.07,0:12:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,How are we supposed to\Nwipe him out? You're not.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.47,0:12:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It makes me invincible.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.83,0:12:43.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Next I'll attack your\Nmaster of dragons, soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.53,0:12:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, my Ori-Kalcos Giygas!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.77,0:12:51.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice try, but my dragon's too strong!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.51,0:12:57.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You Tora!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.27,0:12:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Absorb all the damage!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.77,0:13:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My life points are safe,\Nand now my Giygas returns!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.85,0:13:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That Kree, he's letting Azorichalcos\NGygus get its butt kicked on purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.23,0:13:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,so it can come back stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.31,0:13:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That can't be it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.83,0:13:20.93,Default,,0,0,0,,His monster would have\Nto be destroyed seven
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.01,0:13:23.45,Default,,0,0,0,,more times before it\Ncould defeat my dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.53,0:13:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,So there must be more to his plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.49,0:13:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps the secret lies in his cutora\Nand its ability to absorb attack damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.47,0:13:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, that creature must have\Nanother special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.27,0:13:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, darts, my move!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.13,0:13:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as that eyesore is on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.75,0:13:45.41,Default,,0,0,0,,it's pointless to attack\NIzzoricalco's Giygas,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.49,0:13:47.90,Default,,0,0,0,,because darts won't lose any life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.21,0:13:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, Giygas will just come back stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.79,0:13:55.15,Default,,0,0,0,,But if I attack darts directly,\NI should be able to win the duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.45,0:13:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I place one card face down on the field!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.23,0:14:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And next, I summon my Blade Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.25,0:14:11.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And since I have only\None card left in my hand,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.75,0:14:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Blade Knight gets another\N400 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.35,0:14:19.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I think that'll do for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.15,0:14:22.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He's setting himself up for something.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.87,0:14:25.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi better not screw this up for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.45,0:14:27.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to pick up where I left off!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.79,0:14:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.31,0:14:33.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sacrificing my Blade\NKnight to activate this card!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.49,0:14:35.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Reflect energy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.01,0:14:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Yuge,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.69,0:14:46.75,Default,,0,0,0,,it's up to you to blow this freak\Nshow away with your Dragon Soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.93,0:14:47.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Once you attack,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.29,0:14:50.93,Default,,0,0,0,,my Reflect Energy\NSatellite will redirect the
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.01,0:14:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,blast to his light\Npoints and wipe him out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.11,0:14:54.97,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.35,0:14:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Dragon Soldier, attack\Nwith Dragon Saber Blast!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.73,0:15:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.79,0:15:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They were able to flatten\Nthat freak together!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.79,0:15:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course they were!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.23,0:15:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.71,0:15:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,That attack was supposed to\Nhit darts, not his monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.41,0:15:24.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a force field!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.19,0:15:26.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But how did he create it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.99,0:15:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,By using the second layer\Nof the seal, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.55,0:15:36.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever my life points are targeted, my\NOricalcos Deutero steps in to defend me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.21,0:15:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It's simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.17,0:15:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I make a sacrifice so that\Nyour monster takes the hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.57,0:15:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what that means, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.15,0:15:47.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Your dragon just attacked itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.13,0:15:54.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh! Do something!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.03,0:15:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my diffusion!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.03,0:16:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Talk about luck of the draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.27,0:16:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.63,0:16:08.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It's through teamwork and determination\Nthat we have avoided your attacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.81,0:16:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You have a little speech for\Neverything, don't you, Pharaoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.37,0:16:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You must get so tired of\Nbeing right all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.25,0:16:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, don't worry, because\Nthat all ends here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.93,0:16:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,So listen closely as I teach\Nyou a little lesson of my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.87,0:16:27.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And I assure you, it has nothing\Nto do with teamwork or friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.17,0:16:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And it all starts with this, a magic\Ncard known as Orichalcos Mirror.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.27,0:16:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Now all I have to do is\Nsacrifice a monster from
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.37,0:16:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,my hand in order to summon\Nmy Mirror Knight Calling,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.07,0:16:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,which in turn calls four knights\Nto the field to protect me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.99,0:16:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He played four monsters in one turn?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.89,0:16:51.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You poor fools.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.85,0:16:54.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll never get past Mirror Knights.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.85,0:17:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,And thanks to my Oricalcos Deuteros, I\Ngained 3,000 more life points. That's insane.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.91,0:17:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, pay close attention\Nto the mirror's reflection.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.71,0:17:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.51,0:17:12.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Each knight reflects something or\Nsomeone on your side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.31,0:17:15.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That dictates the value\Nof their attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.67,0:17:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,So that means...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.99,0:17:17.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, it does.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.27,0:17:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,My knights receive the same number\Nof attack points as their target.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.89,0:17:38.72,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.01,0:17:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Scared of your own reflections?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.05,0:17:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as my Mirror Knight\NCalling Crystal is on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.35,0:17:50.70,Default,,0,0,0,,my monster's shields will always return.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.13,0:17:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means my Mirror\NKnights can't be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.57,0:17:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,So go ahead and summon\Nwhatever you'd like.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.19,0:17:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.49,0:18:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,But first, I think I'll\Nactivate my card of Demise.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.31,0:18:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me draw five new cards, as long\Nas I discard my entire hand in five turns.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.75,0:18:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's worth it, for a fresh start.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.63,0:18:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll play my Silent Doom card,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.93,0:18:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,so I can summon a monster\Nfrom my grave in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.27,0:18:21.51,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose Blade Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.03,0:18:28.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, I sacrifice Blade Knight\Nin order to summon Kaiser Glider!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.89,0:18:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And last, I'll place one card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.61,0:18:35.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I must say, I'm impressed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.05,0:18:40.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Kaiser Glider is safe from any monster\Nwith the same number of attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.35,0:18:42.59,Default,,0,0,0,,So my knights can't crush it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.45,0:18:45.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba may be safe for now,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.27,0:18:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,but we need to find a way to destroy\Nhis monsters, not hide from them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.37,0:18:52.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, darts, my move.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.67,0:18:57.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Mirror Force, this should help.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.81,0:19:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll place one card face down,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.57,0:19:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,and then I'll summon my big shield\NGardner to the field in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.11,0:19:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.41,0:19:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,How pathetic. Now then,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.05,0:19:14.65,Default,,0,0,0,,since it's the start of a new turn for\Nme, I gain another 3,000 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.41,0:19:17.61,Default,,0,0,0,,We must stop him and fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.91,0:19:19.07,Default,,0,0,0,,When Darts attacks,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.37,0:19:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll activate my mirror force to counteract\Nhis mirrors and destroy his knights.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.53,0:19:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, folks.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.87,0:19:27.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my trap card.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.83,0:19:33.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Your knights are only safe if your mirror\Nknight calling magic card is in play.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.21,0:19:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,So now, I'll squash it\Nwith Ring of Destruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.91,0:19:52.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, when your knights are\Ndestroyed, they can't come back!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.63,0:20:00.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.99,0:20:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.75,0:20:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Recognize anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.67,0:20:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi! But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.19,0:20:12.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I control the souls of\Nyour companions, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.97,0:20:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Let them go!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.83,0:20:19.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack my knights and you'll\Nbe attacking your friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.15,0:20:22.55,Default,,0,0,0,,If I had played my mirror force,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.91,0:20:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,that would mean my friends would\Nbe gone forever by my own hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.05,0:20:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what you do, you lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.81,0:20:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's impossible to defeat me\Nwithout destroying these monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.79,0:20:40.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And you can't destroy my knights without\Ndestroying the souls of your friends.
